Change(genesis='66602cd0dec37d58d03eec9518ca805a7ac38ea912d2b0c366a0b67b4b9f50b6', deps=('3f85de5b1d6f1422afcac5e13d569c3baaf3a45c6f1fc685ed3e65099f150e00',), event=Revised(decision='train', at=datetime(2026, 11, 22, 2, 32, 38, 686783), actor='assistant', title='The merge queue is scripts/train.sh; reviewed PRs ride a train and nobody merges a train by hand', body='*The merge queue is* `scripts/train.sh`: reviewed pull requests ride a TRAIN. `build <pr>...` merges them onto `train` from `origin/master` in an order that is a function of their heads: a PR whose head holds more of the others\' merges first, so a stacked PR\'s merge carries its base, and the head\'s name orders the rest. A PR\'s changelog entry is its own fragment, `changelog.d/<branch>.md`, and the release cut folds the fragments into the version\'s section and deletes them, so no two PRs edit one hunk; `app/Cargo.lock` keeps the train\'s side and cargo adds the PR\'s; any other conflict is skipped for its author. `gate --remote github` runs the tree half on core\'s runners (the train commit\'s public tree, once its leak guard passes, pushed to core\'s `gate/<train sha>`) and the live half on the box, keeping each verdict in `.git/train/` keyed by half and tree. A VERDICT IS OF WHAT IT READ (2026-11-22): a live row names a digest of the stores beside the instance file, taken before the run (a hash alone); a land reads the live half at its newest row\'s digest, a red and a green are a finding only at one digest, and a finding lands nothing; the land prints every set-aside and each red the stores moved past. A red traced to a cause outside the tree is set aside only at a terminal (`set-aside <half> --because <task> "<words>"`), naming one row and an open or completed roadmap task; a red nobody set aside beside a green at its digest is still a finding. The growth check runs before the halves: an undeclared growth, a malformed declaration or a change that writes `reading` refuses the train with no row, and a check that compared nothing lets the halves go on and fails the nightly. `nightly` runs both halves in full on master. `bisect` finds the merge that turned a half red. `land` pushes master only from a HEAD both halves passed, then publishes it; `scripts/deploy.sh <rev>` is the operator\'s. A STACKED PR branches from its base PR\'s branch and lands with it or after it. Nobody merges a train by hand.', rationale="Decided 2026-10-03: GitHub's merge queue is for organisations, and the gate is the box's. Revised 2026-11-06: the changelog is fragments (#360), the Codespace remote is gone (#336), and the nightly full gate exists. Restated 2026-11-22: a verdict is of what it read (the live row's digest, the set-aside, the growth check before the halves).", supersedes=()))